, this Court  summarised some categories of cases where  Patna High Court CR. MISC. No.51439 of 2016 dt.16-05-2024  6/8  inherent power can and should be exercised  to quash the proceedings : (AIR p. 869, para  6)
 (i) where it manifestly appears that there is a  legal bar against the institution or  continuance e.g. want of sanction;
 (ii) where the allegations in the first information  report or complaint taken at its face value  and accepted in their entirety do not  constitute the offence alleged;
 (iii) where the allegations constitute an offence,
 but there is no legal evidence adduced or the  evidence adduced clearly or manifestly fails to  prove the charge.
